@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] guest-image-identity
A Linux guest artifact MUST contain an x86-64 uncompressed ELF kernel, its
matching initrd and a rootfs assembled from the named distribution's pinned
release inputs. Manifests MUST record SHA-256 and byte lengths of those exact
artifacts. Linux images use version 4 and declare source protocol 2 only when
their workspace receiver is enabled at boot, otherwise null. Native FreeBSD and
illumos images use version 6 with the pinned CloudHv firmware and raw-GPT disk;
the FreeBSD disk retains its EFI and UFS partitions. Every native manifest MUST
record exact artifact sizes and digests plus the positive kernel byte count,
SHA-256, full source revision, patch/configuration hashes and compiler identity.
A source/build receipt with unavailable kernel bytes MUST NOT produce an image
or enter the fleet catalog. Firmware-booted Windows images use
version 5, or version 7 only for the separate Windows editor candidate, under
the `windows/CONTRACTS` identity contract (ADR-0170).
Editor-capable images MUST additionally record the immutable protocol/source/patch
release descriptor and at least 2 GiB writable disk headroom. The immutable rootfs
is a template for a separate writable VM disk. See ADR-0011 and ADR-0016.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;protocol] guest-git-identity-capability
Linux and Windows image builders MUST declare git_identity_version 1 only when
the current Git identity writer, system configuration include and an enabled
workspace identity writer are installed in the image. The writer MAY be the
generic workspace receiver or a profile-owned writer such as Inception's
guest-owned bootstrap; images without an enabled writer MUST omit the
capability. Existing immutable native artifacts MUST NOT acquire it without a
separately rebuilt, reviewed and admitted exact image. New native candidates MAY
explicitly declare version 1 only with source-v2, the current attribution writer
and system include in the enabled native payload; their declaration MUST NOT
change promoted pins or imply native admission before exact qualification.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] native-agent-payload
FreeBSD and illumos image builders MAY copy a reviewed native-agent payload only
when its binaries are built from the pinned Lyra source and the manifest declares
the matching native agent set. A workspace source version 2 MUST NOT be emitted
without that payload and a corresponding guest service definition. Copying a
binary into an image does not by itself establish readiness, trust, terminal,
workspace, SSH or execution capability; those claims require boot-bound daemon
responses and runtime evidence.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] foreign-linux-runtime-closure
Arch and RPM based foreign Linux images MUST carry the pinned Lyra and terminald
guest binaries, readiness/network/resize scripts, Python, Git, OpenSSH, sudo,
certificate bundle and every referenced runtime closure path. Their systemd units
MUST use explicit FHS links under /usr and /usr/local, and image assembly MUST NOT
invoke a distribution package manager or fetch network content.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] foreign-linux-service-boundaries
Foreign Linux images with private service roots MUST enable generic Linux trustd,
workspaced, roster-bound SSH, private DNS, readiness and terminal units. Trust and
network ordering MUST precede readiness; workspace cloning MUST remain outside the
readiness dependency set. Images without private roots MUST leave those listeners
disabled while retaining the serial-login and root-login fences.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] guest-console-access-boundary
Guest PTY access MUST be mediated by Marshall's authenticated terminal authority
and Lilly's boot-bound vsock gate. Serial output MUST remain read-only without
root autologin. Guest SSH MUST deny root login, require a current per-user account
roster from the private Audi service before sshd starts, and authorize each
offered key against the current VM, account and Cedar grant. SSH MUST be
public-key only, use certified per-boot host keys kept only in volatile runtime
storage (/run on Linux and /var/run/overalls on native guests), and remain behind Audi's VM-bound
authorization. User homes MUST survive account deactivation.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] guest-network-address-scope
Guest networking MUST accept only one validated `lilly.ipv4` parameter from the
10.10, 10.20, 10.30 or 10.40 profile ranges, excluding reserved endpoints. It MUST use
/32 addresses and a host gateway route; DHCP and IPv6 MUST remain disabled.
Inception MUST also derive its Audi address in 10.41 at exactly the same slot.
Other profiles MUST NOT receive a secondary address.
The guest configuration alone MUST NOT be treated as sibling/host isolation;
the host's routing and nftables policy supply that boundary under ADR-0015.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment;recovery] android-emulator-guest-identity
The Android emulator guest MUST be a Linux version-4 guest artifact assembled from
the pinned Android SDK/system-image closure. Its emulator service MUST run with
software rendering and no accelerator, and its AVD state MUST live under a
systemd-managed writable state directory separate from the immutable image root.
The service MUST fail closed if ADB does not report `sys.boot_completed=1` within
the fixed 600-second startup budget.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] android-display-ingress
The Android emulator's RFB server MUST bind only to guest loopback. A separate
typed relay MAY bind the fixed guest display port, but MUST validate Lilly's
bounded display preface before forwarding and MUST NOT expose RFB or ADB as a
public listener or claim browser authentication.
